{title: O Love That Wilt Not Let Me Go}
{artist: George Matheson / Albert L. Peace}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: G}
{key_original: Ab}
{tempo: 100}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (The Hymnbook (Richmond, Virginia: Presbyterian Church in the United States, 1955), # 400)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]O Love that wilt not let me go,__[D7]__
[D7]I rest my weary soul in thee;
[D7]I [G]give thee [B]back the life I [E]owe,__[Em]__
[Em]That [A7]in thine ocean depths its [G]flow__[D]__
[D]May richer, [G]full__[D7]__er [G]be.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]O Joy that seekest me through pain,__[D7]__
[D7]I cannot close my heart to thee;
[D7]I [G]trace the [B]rainbow through the [E]rain,__[Em]__
[Em]And [A7]feel the promise is not [G]vain,__[D]__
[D]That morn shall [G]tear__[D7]__less [G]be.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]O Cross that liftest up my head,__[D7]__
[D7]I dare not ask to fly from thee;
[D7]I [G]lay in [B]dust life’s glory [E]dead,__[Em]__
[Em]And [A7]from the ground there blossoms [G]red__[D]__
[D]Life that shall [G]end__[D7]__less [G]be.
{end_of_verse}
